Author: Michele Dipace (@kaffeine1)

Kaffeine experimental ARM64 preview

Double-click Test-JIT to run the original 68k file test with the requested
Kaffeine JIT backend, or Test-Moira for an interpreter comparison.
The test writes a small text file, closes it, reopens it and checks every
byte. A PASS and rc 0 describe this test only.

The preview starts with a requested JIT default in RAM. Actual backend
messages and JIT counters are in the host session's two serial logs.
Keep those messages when reporting a backend-specific problem.

For your own imported application, open Applications/Imported. Some apps
need a Shell launch, assigns or additional libraries; follow their own
instructions and record your launch method. In a Shell use:

  Stack 1048576
  Set KAFFEINE_CPU jit
  SYS:KaffeinePreview/Applications/Imported/YourProgram

Repeat with Set KAFFEINE_CPU moira to compare. Use a new document, save it,
close and reopen it, and check its contents. Results are retained in this
session's disk, not in the package's original disk.

Close applications before closing the VM. The host launcher limits each
session to 15 minutes by default. Read the host README for changing the
limit and for creating a local report. Inspect a report before sharing it.
No report is uploaded automatically; application and document files are
not collected in reports.

This QEMU preview is experimental. A successful test is not a promise that
all 68k applications or physical Raspberry Pi models are compatible.
